From: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.cz>
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] btrfs: kill key type helpers
Date: Wed,  5 Oct 2011 12:22:13 +0200
Message-ID: <d376fde640c87de6355a1a39d3faade62c09f280.1317746378.git.dsterba@suse.cz>
References: <cover.1317746377.git.dsterba@suse.cz>
Cc: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.cz>
To: linux-btrfs@vger.kernel.org
Return-path: <linux-btrfs-owner@vger.kernel.org>
In-Reply-To: <cover.1317746377.git.dsterba@suse.cz>
List-ID: <linux-btrfs.vger.kernel.org>

btrfs_set_key_type and btrfs_key_type are used inconsistently along with
open coded variants. Other members of btrfs_key are accessed directly
without any helpers anyway.

Generated by spatch:
<Smpl>
@setkeyaddr@
expression KEY, VALUE;
@@
- btrfs_set_key_type(&KEY, VALUE)
+ KEY.type = VALUE

@setkeyptr@
expression KEY, VALUE;
@@
- btrfs_set_key_type(KEY, VALUE)
+ KEY->type = VALUE

@getkeyaddr@
expression KEY;
@@
- btrfs_key_type(&KEY)
+ KEY.type

@getkeyexpr@
expression KEY;
identifier IDX;
@@
- btrfs_key_type(KEY+IDX)
+ KEY[IDX].type

@getkeyptr@
expression KEY;
@@
- btrfs_key_type(KEY)
+ KEY->type

@setkillproto@
type T;
@@
- T btrfs_set_key_type(...) {
- ...
- }

@getkillproto@
type T;
@@
- T btrfs_key_type(...) {
- ...
- }
</Smpl>

Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.cz>
